# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify header rules.
#
# LOCK 4 OF 4 on a concept build. The other three are robots.txt Disallow, the
# absent sitemap, and the six-directive <meta name="robots">.
#
# X-Robots-Tag matters because the meta tag only exists inside an HTML document.
# It does not protect the job photographs, the OG image, the favicon or the web
# manifest — all of which are separate URLs on this host, all of which are
# crawlable on their own, and one of which is a set of a real business's project
# photos. A response header covers every one of them.
#
# Kept deliberately redundant with the meta tag: they fail differently. A
# misconfigured host silently drops these rules, and a proxy or a reader-mode
# extraction can strip the <head>. Either lock alone would leave a gap.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex, notranslate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Belt and braces on the two paths a crawler is most likely to reach directly.
/robots.txt
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/*.jpg
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, noimageindex, noarchive

/*.png
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, noimageindex, noarchive

/*.avif
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, noimageindex, noarchive

/*.webp
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, noimageindex, noarchive
